-[Guy] No pressure.
-[Heather chuckles] Maya.

232
00:09:48,713 --> 00:09:51,632
[Maya] So, Sam told me he wants
a nice family-friendly house.

233
00:09:51,716 --> 00:09:54,635
So I thought Nichols Canyon 
could be perfect.

234
00:09:54,719 --> 00:09:56,387
It's a beautiful house, 
let's check it out.

235
00:10:00,308 --> 00:10:02,643
[Heather] Four bedrooms, three bathrooms.

236
00:10:02,727 --> 00:10:04,061
So, it's a good size.

237
00:10:04,645 --> 00:10:07,398
This is the living area,
newly remodeled actually.

238
00:10:07,773 --> 00:10:09,150
[Sam] I love the light.

239
00:10:09,233 --> 00:10:12,069
-[Heather] Do you guys cook?
-[Maya] This is where the magic happens.

240
00:10:12,153 --> 00:10:14,572
I wasn't talking about 
having sex on the counter.

241
00:10:14,655 --> 00:10:16,157
-Just the cooking.
-[all chuckling]

242
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:17,825
Wait, the magic happens on the counter?

243
00:10:18,284 --> 00:10:21,495
Not anymore, not after having a baby,
barely any magic happens.

244
00:10:21,579 --> 00:10:23,205
-Just the cooking now.
-[all laughing]

245
00:10:26,709 --> 00:10:28,085
[Maya] What do you guys think?

246
00:10:28,169 --> 00:10:29,670
[Sam] It's nice. It's very nice.

247
00:10:29,754 --> 00:10:32,131
-We just have to talk about the commute.
-The commute.

248
00:10:32,214 --> 00:10:34,634
-It can be bad.
-We're used to the center.

249
00:10:34,717 --> 00:10:37,053
Have you heard of, like, online shopping?
I'm kidding. [chuckles]

250
00:10:37,678 --> 00:10:39,388
[Maya] Okay, let's see the bedrooms.

251
00:10:39,472 --> 00:10:42,433
This is your master, which is a good size.

252
00:10:43,184 --> 00:10:44,894
-[Sam] Yeah. Wow.
-[Maya] So nice.

253
00:10:44,977 --> 00:10:47,188
-[Guy] So cute.
-[Sam] This actually is a big back yard

254
00:10:47,271 --> 00:10:49,899
-for the Hollywood Hills.
-[Sam] There's succulents over here.

255
00:10:49,982 --> 00:10:51,817
[Guy] A lot of potential. It's beautiful.

256
00:10:51,901 --> 00:10:54,320
-You can get a dog first.
-[Sam laughing]

257
00:10:54,403 --> 00:10:55,821
-[Maya] Maybe a baby.
-[Guy] Yeah.

258
00:10:55,905 --> 00:10:57,990
It's not my place to tell you what to get
and when,

259
00:10:58,074 --> 00:11:00,743
but I feel like it's a great 
starter family home.

260
00:11:00,826 --> 00:11:01,994
We're back.

261
00:11:02,078 --> 00:11:04,038
Hey! What do you guys think?

262
00:11:04,121 --> 00:11:05,581
-I like it a lot.
-You like it?

263
00:11:05,665 --> 00:11:07,333
-Yes.
-You like the vibe?

264
00:11:07,416 --> 00:11:09,001
-We do.
-And the vibe is good.

265
00:11:09,418 --> 00:11:11,212
The light, the floors,

266
00:11:11,295 --> 00:11:12,880
the skylights, the windows...

267
00:11:12,963 --> 00:11:14,882
-[Sam] It has a lot of good features.
-Yeah.

268
00:11:14,965 --> 00:11:17,551
Everything is perfect, 
the only minor thing is...

269
00:11:18,386 --> 00:11:19,720
driving up the hill.

270
00:11:19,804 --> 00:11:21,514
-Oh... yes.
-[Guy] Yes.

271
00:11:21,597 --> 00:11:23,599
We're hard workers. She drove from the OC,

272
00:11:23,683 --> 00:11:25,601
-I flew from Miami this morning.
-I know.

273
00:11:25,685 --> 00:11:27,728
Just for you to tell me it's not for us.

274
00:11:27,812 --> 00:11:31,190
-So I guess we have to buy it then.
-No pressure at all, okay?

275
00:11:31,273 --> 00:11:33,234
[Heather chuckling]

276
00:11:33,317 --> 00:11:35,319
♪ The pressure never got me
Got Me ♪

277
00:11:35,403 --> 00:11:38,030
♪ I love it in the hot seat
Hot seat ♪

278
00:11:38,239 --> 00:11:39,990
♪ I'm gonna put on a show
What ♪

279
00:11:40,074 --> 00:11:41,867
♪ I'm gonna make sure you know ♪

280
00:11:41,951 --> 00:11:44,453
♪ That I'm a getter
I'm a getter... ♪

281
00:11:45,371 --> 00:11:48,082
[Maya] What's up
with all the mosquitos in LA by the way?

282
00:11:48,165 --> 00:11:49,542
I get bitten so much.

283
00:11:50,042 --> 00:11:53,212
And we're selling all these houses
where whole walls disappear.

284
00:11:53,295 --> 00:11:55,256
-So that's really not good.
-[Mary and Chrishell chuckling]

285
00:11:55,339 --> 00:11:57,591
I'm surprised you're getting
bit out here, Maya.

286
00:11:57,717 --> 00:12:01,095
-[Chrishell] Maybe you're extra sweet.
-I know, I guess. I have nice blood.

287
00:12:01,178 --> 00:12:03,180
-Hello.
-[Brett] How are you, bud?

288
00:12:03,806 --> 00:12:05,057
-[Chrishell] Hey, Guy.
-Good to see you, man.

289
00:12:05,141 --> 00:12:06,183
-You, too.
-[Brett] Yeah.

290
00:12:06,809 --> 00:12:08,769
-You here to see, Chrishell?
-Hi!

291
00:12:08,894 --> 00:12:10,271
-[Guy] Hey, what's up?
-How're you doing?

292
00:12:10,354 --> 00:12:12,022
-It's hot out there, right?
-Yeah.

293
00:12:12,106 --> 00:12:13,357
You wanna sit?

294
00:12:13,816 --> 00:12:15,317
[Chrishell]
Do you want any water or anything?

295
00:12:15,401 --> 00:12:17,862
[Guy] I'm good.
Actually, hopefully this'll be quick.

296
00:12:17,945 --> 00:12:20,823
Just wanna see what's going on,
why my house is not selling.

297
00:12:21,407 --> 00:12:23,492
It's been on the market with you guys,

298
00:12:23,576 --> 00:12:25,244
you've had it for two months now and...

299
00:12:25,327 --> 00:12:27,413
-I got nothing.
-[Chrishell] I know.

300
00:12:27,496 --> 00:12:30,207
The only person that wants to sell this
more than you is me.

301
00:12:30,291 --> 00:12:33,461
So, I promise you I have 
your best interests at heart.

302
00:12:33,544 --> 00:12:36,380
I do think it'd be a good idea
to come down a little on the price

303
00:12:36,464 --> 00:12:39,800
just because when I look
at what else is on the market

304
00:12:39,884 --> 00:12:42,470
and comps in the area,
price per square foot is a little lower.

305
00:12:42,553 --> 00:12:44,096
I don't think square feet is lower.

306
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:47,808
I mean, you're getting views, 
a great yard, a very nice house.

307
00:12:47,892 --> 00:12:50,478
Price per square feet,
they're getting a deal.

308
00:12:50,561 --> 00:12:53,606
The house is gorgeous. It's absolutely
stunning. You did an amazing job.

309
00:12:53,689 --> 00:12:55,608
But the ball is in the buyer's court

310
00:12:55,691 --> 00:12:57,193
and it just... [inhales deeply]

311
00:12:57,276 --> 00:12:59,153
You know, especially at this price point,

312
00:12:59,236 --> 00:13:02,698
they know they have the power,
and there's a lot of inventory.

313
00:13:02,781 --> 00:13:05,618
No house ever comes 
without any challenges,

314
00:13:05,701 --> 00:13:08,120
but this one has definitely 
had quite a few.

315
00:13:08,621 --> 00:13:10,790
I've had to deal with a barking dog,

316
00:13:10,873 --> 00:13:13,459
some very cranky neighbors,

317
00:13:13,542 --> 00:13:17,379
and we happen to be right 
underneath a huge flight path.

318
00:13:17,713 --> 00:13:21,884
It's one of those things where if you're
open to maybe dropping it slightly,

319
00:13:21,967 --> 00:13:23,344
I think it's the best move.

320
00:13:24,470 --> 00:13:26,347
-Uh...
-Let's-- Chrishell is creating

321
00:13:26,430 --> 00:13:27,723
an efficient market place.

322
00:13:27,807 --> 00:13:31,644
-We've held it open every single Sunday.
-[Chrishell] Every Sunday.

323
00:13:31,727 --> 00:13:34,021
There's nobody out there
that doesn't know about the house.

324
00:13:34,104 --> 00:13:35,731
So, there's nothing left but price.

325
00:13:35,814 --> 00:13:40,361
And I do think a lot of times when
you're putting in your search keys,

326
00:13:40,444 --> 00:13:43,614
what if it's not even coming up
on someone's search because...

327
00:13:43,697 --> 00:13:46,242
4.5 is their absolute max,
or something like that

328
00:13:46,325 --> 00:13:47,326
if they're typing it in.

329
00:13:47,409 --> 00:13:50,538
The difference between people
that are buying up to four million

330
00:13:50,621 --> 00:13:54,375
to the difference of people buying
up to five, you know, in the Valley,

331
00:13:54,458 --> 00:13:58,379
-our pool drops by a significant amount.
-Yeah, yeah.

332
00:13:58,462 --> 00:14:01,048
[Jason] By the way, I hate to interject,

333
00:14:01,131 --> 00:14:03,300
but I like the idea
of a $200,000 reduction

334
00:14:03,384 --> 00:14:06,345
because, guess what, we might be having
this conversation again in a month.

335
00:14:06,428 --> 00:14:09,348
We'll have just shot ourselves in the foot
and wasted a $100,000 reduction.

336
00:14:09,431 --> 00:14:11,433
-We might as well go for it.
-I agree.

337
00:14:11,725 --> 00:14:13,435
[Guy] I mean, it kills me
to even make a reduction.

338
00:14:13,519 --> 00:14:17,231
Even a $100,000. 
$200,000 is more than I want.

339
00:14:17,314 --> 00:14:20,734
I can meet you guys half way
if you want, we can go 4.499.

340
00:14:20,818 --> 00:14:23,404
Get under that price point, you know,
under the 4.5...

341
00:14:23,487 --> 00:14:25,364
I like 4.399.

342
00:14:29,201 --> 00:14:32,037
-No, I'm not ready for that.
-[both laughing]

343
00:14:33,038 --> 00:14:35,291
-All right.
-Alrighty, what else are we going to do?

344
00:14:35,374 --> 00:14:37,710
[Jason] I think if we can get
a price reduction,

345
00:14:37,793 --> 00:14:42,006
I think that that justifies us
redoubling our marketing dollars.

346
00:14:42,089 --> 00:14:44,216
Fair is fair, we'll do everything again.

347
00:14:44,300 --> 00:14:47,511
We'll take the full page ad out,
we'll do new open houses,

348
00:14:47,595 --> 00:14:49,013
we'll do new broker opens.

349
00:14:49,096 --> 00:14:52,433
That'll resend it out to everybody,
it's now back in their inbox,

350
00:14:52,516 --> 00:14:55,853
I get to call all those people
that have expressed interest

351
00:14:55,936 --> 00:14:58,063
that saw it in the past.
Every single person now,

352
00:14:58,147 --> 00:15:00,858
I get to call them up and be like,
"Let me show it to you again."

353
00:15:00,941 --> 00:15:04,194
But we can't keep remarketing
every time we get $100,000.

354
00:15:04,278 --> 00:15:07,281
We can't keep throwing money
and time at this.

355
00:15:07,364 --> 00:15:11,452
That's not in my hands. I'm just relying
on you guys to move this forward,

356
00:15:11,535 --> 00:15:14,038
and hopefully close it, 
and get that buyer there.

357
00:15:14,121 --> 00:15:15,414
[Chrishell] All right, sounds good.

358
00:15:15,497 --> 00:15:16,957
-Thank you, Guy.
-[Guy] Nice seeing you again.

359
00:15:17,041 --> 00:15:19,585
You too. Maybe when we see each other,

360
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:21,629
-it'll be on better terms.
-I hope so.

361
00:15:21,712 --> 00:15:23,422
-I really do.
-Okay, I'll talk to you soon.

362
00:15:23,505 --> 00:15:24,465
All right, bye.

363
00:15:24,548 --> 00:15:25,382
Thank you.

364
00:15:26,717 --> 00:15:28,260
[Jason] So, 4.499?

365
00:15:29,136 --> 00:15:31,263
-[Chrishell] Yeah.
-[Jason] Okay, I mean it's better.

366
00:15:31,347 --> 00:15:35,184
Between you and me, we're gonna end up
at 4.299 or 4.399 before that thing sells.

367
00:15:35,267 --> 00:15:37,937
I've a feeling that's not gonna be
our last conversation with him.

368
00:15:38,312 --> 00:15:39,813
-About this.
-Oh, please God.

369
00:15:40,147 --> 00:15:42,524
[Jason] We should give him
another broker open with an ad.

370
00:15:42,775 --> 00:15:44,068
-With the new price? Okay.
-Yeah.

371
00:15:44,151 --> 00:15:45,110
[Jason] Thanks.

372
00:15:45,194 --> 00:15:48,030
Those aren't fun conversations, Chrishell,
but thanks for getting through it

373
00:15:48,113 --> 00:15:49,531
-and handling it well.
-[Chrishell sighs]

374
00:15:49,615 --> 00:15:53,786
[Maya speaking Hebrew]

375
00:15:53,869 --> 00:15:56,163
-Hey, pretty lady.
-Hey, how are you?

376
00:15:56,288 --> 00:15:57,915
You look like a ray of sunshine.

377
00:15:58,207 --> 00:15:59,166
-[Heather] Hi.
-Hi, guys.

378
00:15:59,249 --> 00:16:01,293
-[Brett] What's up, baby? How are you?
-[Christine] You look great, Amanza.

379
00:16:01,377 --> 00:16:03,545
-Thank you.
-[Maya] I need to get my nails done.

380
00:16:04,046 --> 00:16:05,839
I just got mine done.
Look, they have holes in them.

381
00:16:06,423 --> 00:16:08,425
-[Heather] Uh-oh.
-What?

382
00:16:08,634 --> 00:16:09,802
[Heather] No, shoot.

383
00:16:09,885 --> 00:16:12,805
My client Collin he's
like, super, super busy,

384
00:16:12,888 --> 00:16:15,307
and I'm supposed to show him
a house on Doheny.

385
00:16:15,974 --> 00:16:18,477
And the only day he can do it
is this Saturday at four

386
00:16:18,560 --> 00:16:21,438
and I have Tarek's daughter's 
birthday party.

387
00:16:21,855 --> 00:16:22,982
-[Heather] There's...
-[straw gurgling]

388
00:16:23,065 --> 00:16:24,608
If I miss her birthday,

389
00:16:24,692 --> 00:16:26,610
she'll be so upset,
there's no way I can miss it.

390
00:16:26,694 --> 00:16:30,322
I'd totally do it, 
but I'm flying 9 a.m. to Miami.

391
00:16:30,823 --> 00:16:31,991
[Christine groaning]

392
00:16:32,074 --> 00:16:33,242
-Christine?
-No.

393
00:16:33,909 --> 00:16:35,953
Christine...
What do you really have going on?

394
00:16:36,036 --> 00:16:37,121
[Christine] I'm busy.

395
00:16:37,204 --> 00:16:38,872
She's busy booking her next vacation.

396
00:16:38,956 --> 00:16:42,418
-[Heather] Christine, seriously...
-I can't, I have a nail appointment.

397
00:16:42,501 --> 00:16:44,128
Like, at 4 o'clock?

398
00:16:44,211 --> 00:16:45,546
-[Christine] Yeah.
-[Maya chuckles]

399
00:16:45,629 --> 00:16:48,382
No, my nail girl is busy. 
She does Ariana Grande, too.

400
00:16:48,465 --> 00:16:50,926
Jason, you wanna show 
Heather's listing on Doheny?

401
00:16:51,010 --> 00:16:52,594
-No, I'm good.
-[Heather] Jason!

402
00:16:53,012 --> 00:16:55,472
I have Tarek's daughter's birthday,
I cannot miss.

403
00:16:55,848 --> 00:16:57,933
You wouldn't know, 
you have no children in your life.

404
00:16:58,016 --> 00:16:59,935
-I'm not commenting.
-[Heather] You guys, like, really?

405
00:17:00,019 --> 00:17:02,396
How many times have I helped you guys out?

406
00:17:02,479 --> 00:17:04,690
-[Heather] Chrishell?
-I'm doing this... I'm sorry,

407
00:17:04,773 --> 00:17:05,941
a client I'm showing.

408
00:17:06,024 --> 00:17:07,359
[Heather] You guys, anyone else?

409
00:17:07,443 --> 00:17:09,570
-[Amanza] Where is the property?
-Doheny.

410
00:17:09,653 --> 00:17:11,864
[Heather] It's really important
that he sees it 'cause

411
00:17:11,947 --> 00:17:14,450
I don't know if I can get him
in for another month or something.

412
00:17:14,533 --> 00:17:15,576
I mean, I have the kid.

413
00:17:15,659 --> 00:17:20,164
My daughter has gymnastics 
until two in the Valley, but...

414
00:17:20,247 --> 00:17:21,665
Could you make it by four?

415
00:17:23,709 --> 00:17:26,587
-I think I can make it by four.
-I'll send you all the information.

416
00:17:26,670 --> 00:17:27,755
I'll put you guys in touch.

417
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:30,215
-I don't want to move this on him.
-[straw gurgling]

418
00:17:30,299 --> 00:17:31,133
[Amanza] Okay.

419
00:17:31,216 --> 00:17:32,718
-It's gonna be tight.
-Are you sure?

420
00:17:32,801 --> 00:17:34,845
I'll just drop her off and then go.

421
00:17:35,345 --> 00:17:36,263
Okay.

422
00:17:36,597 --> 00:17:37,723
Yay, everyone wins.

423
00:17:37,806 --> 00:17:39,850
I would really like to make amends 
with Heather,

424
00:17:39,975 --> 00:17:43,187
so I'm hoping that this gesture
will give us a fresh start.

425
00:17:43,270 --> 00:17:45,773
If he buys the house, I'll do something 
for you. How about that?

426
00:17:45,856 --> 00:17:47,900
Twenty-five percent of profit to Amanza.

427
00:17:48,609 --> 00:17:50,903
-Well, let's not get carried away.
-[all laughing]

428
00:17:54,865 --> 00:17:56,033
[Davina] Thank you for coming.

429
00:17:56,116 --> 00:17:58,368
-Thanks for showing it.
-I know, I'm excited to show you.

430
00:17:58,452 --> 00:18:00,287
♪ There's nowhere like ♪

431
00:18:00,370 --> 00:18:02,372
♪ Got the green light ♪

432
00:18:03,665 --> 00:18:05,000
♪ I'm ready to go ♪

433
00:18:05,751 --> 00:18:07,503
♪ I got to go ♪

434
00:18:07,586 --> 00:18:09,338
♪ Watch me now ♪

435
00:18:09,421 --> 00:18:11,215
♪ I'm ready to go ♪

436
00:18:11,298 --> 00:18:12,966
♪ Look out below... ♪

437
00:18:13,050 --> 00:18:15,552
I know selling this house at this price
is really tough.

438
00:18:15,636 --> 00:18:18,222
But I'm up for the challenge,
and I can't fathom the idea 

439
00:18:18,305 --> 00:18:19,973
of Jason telling me, "I told you so."

440
00:18:20,432 --> 00:18:23,560
My friend David is an agent
for a very high-end buyer.

441
00:18:23,644 --> 00:18:25,479
This is a billionaire type of client

442
00:18:25,562 --> 00:18:26,772
and those don't grow on trees.

443
00:18:26,855 --> 00:18:28,899
-[David] More options. Thank you.
-After you.

444
00:18:28,982 --> 00:18:29,858
[David] Ooh, la la.

445
00:18:29,942 --> 00:18:31,777
[Davina] Yeah, does it have a wow factor?

446
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:34,822
Pretty much. You know, we see
a lot of homes, but this is beautiful.

447
00:18:38,117 --> 00:18:40,828
-[David] So the master is downstairs?
-Yes, downstairs.

448
00:18:40,911 --> 00:18:42,371
Yeah, overlooking the pond, very peaceful.

449
00:18:42,454 --> 00:18:43,622
[David] Very zen vibes.

450
00:18:43,705 --> 00:18:46,166
-I like what he's done with the grounds.
-Yeah.

451
00:18:46,250 --> 00:18:48,085
It's nine bedrooms and 12 baths.

452
00:18:48,168 --> 00:18:50,838
And obviously, it has a gorgeous 
guesthouse as well.

453
00:18:50,921 --> 00:18:53,048
-Should be enough bathrooms, I think.
-Yeah, I think so.

454
00:18:53,132 --> 00:18:55,008
-Elevator?
-Yeah, elevator.

455
00:18:55,092 --> 00:18:56,051
[Davina] Yeah.

456
00:18:56,135 --> 00:18:58,220
This is kind of the continuation,
so you feel like

457
00:18:58,303 --> 00:19:00,222
you're in the living room,
but you're outdoors.

458
00:19:00,305 --> 00:19:02,182
-[David] Very resort-like.
-Exactly, right?

459
00:19:02,266 --> 00:19:04,351
[Davina] Very LA. 
So, tell me about your client.

460
00:19:05,227 --> 00:19:06,145
The client,

461
00:19:06,228 --> 00:19:08,397
-without saying much, is a family friend.
-Yeah.

462
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:10,274
-He's in biotech.
-Uh-huh. Oh, okay.

463
00:19:10,357 --> 00:19:11,900
You know, obviously a billionaire.

464
00:19:11,984 --> 00:19:12,901
-Yeah.
-So...

465
00:19:12,985 --> 00:19:15,696
-[David] Easily can afford it.
-I love this guy already.

466
00:19:15,988 --> 00:19:16,822
[David laughing]

467
00:19:16,905 --> 00:19:20,033
But do you think he's flexible
with the price or?

468
00:19:20,117 --> 00:19:22,661
-Um... so...
-He's asking 75, am I right?

469
00:19:22,744 --> 00:19:24,163
He's asking 75 million.

470
00:19:24,913 --> 00:19:26,623
-16,000 square feet home.
-Yeah.

471
00:19:26,707 --> 00:19:28,250
Prime Beverly Hills.

472
00:19:28,333 --> 00:19:30,127
Who came up with the price? You or...

473
00:19:30,210 --> 00:19:32,296
-The seller?
-He did, the seller did. Yeah.

474
00:19:32,379 --> 00:19:35,507
So, let her have it for 75.

475
00:19:35,591 --> 00:19:36,425
Okay.

476
00:19:36,508 --> 00:19:39,261
-I don't wanna crush your feelings.
-So-- No, I know.

477
00:19:39,344 --> 00:19:41,221
-He's just very firm on his price.
-Right.

478
00:19:41,305 --> 00:19:43,348
But I think that when he sees an offer

479
00:19:43,432 --> 00:19:45,142
he might be more flexible.

480
00:19:45,225 --> 00:19:47,477
-How firm is he?
-I don't wanna offend him either,

481
00:19:47,561 --> 00:19:50,272
but certainly I'd love to at least 
generate an offer to get it going.

482
00:19:50,355 --> 00:19:53,525
You know how people are when they see
an offer they might change their feelings

483
00:19:53,609 --> 00:19:56,028
and their attitude.
Like, What number are you thinking?

484
00:19:56,111 --> 00:19:57,905
-I mean, to be honest with you...
-Yeah.

485
00:19:57,988 --> 00:20:00,574
It's beautifully done. 
Beautiful house, beautiful location.

486
00:20:01,116 --> 00:20:04,119
But I think we're talking mid-50s.

487
00:20:05,787 --> 00:20:06,872
-Yeah. Yeah.
-You know what I mean?

488
00:20:08,206 --> 00:20:09,958
If it's meant to be, it will be.

489
00:20:11,084 --> 00:20:14,213
♪ I've been making millions
And I spend it on the dance floor ♪

490
00:20:14,296 --> 00:20:17,633
♪ Every time I run out
I go out and I just make more ♪

491
00:20:18,759 --> 00:20:22,221
♪ So put some rhythm in your feeling
Till you're moving your feet ♪

492
00:20:22,304 --> 00:20:25,849
♪ Now put your hands up to the ceiling
And get down on the beat ♪

493
00:20:25,933 --> 00:20:28,518
♪ But if it's wrong
And you're feeling like... ♪

494
00:20:28,602 --> 00:20:29,853
♪ And you're feeling... ♪

495
00:20:29,937 --> 00:20:31,230
[door beeping]

496
00:20:38,153 --> 00:20:39,238
[ringing tone]

497
00:20:39,321 --> 00:20:40,489
[on phone] Hi, this is Heather.

498
00:20:40,572 --> 00:20:41,740
Heather, hey. It's Colin.

499
00:20:41,823 --> 00:20:43,408
So, I'm at the house, but nobody is here.

500
00:20:43,492 --> 00:20:44,952
[Heather] Amanza's not there yet?

501
00:20:45,035 --> 00:20:47,871
Nobody's there and I have
a bit of a tight time frame today.

502
00:20:47,955 --> 00:20:49,665
I gotta leave by, like, 5:30 p.m.

503
00:20:50,707 --> 00:20:51,875
[Heather] Oh, my gosh.

504
00:20:51,959 --> 00:20:55,712
Um... she was supposed to be there 
early to meet you, so...

505
00:20:55,796 --> 00:20:57,089
that's not good at all.

506
00:20:57,172 --> 00:20:59,424
I can stay for, like, another 15 minutes.

507
00:20:59,508 --> 00:21:02,344
[Heather] Okay, Colin.
I'm so, so, so sorry.

508
00:21:02,427 --> 00:21:05,055
Let me figure out where she is
and why she's not there yet, okay?

509
00:21:05,138 --> 00:21:06,014
All right. Thanks, Heather.

510
00:21:06,098 --> 00:21:08,225
-Great. I'll keep you posted.
-All right.

511
00:21:08,642 --> 00:21:09,476
-Okay. Bye, Collin.
-Bye.

512
00:21:09,559 --> 00:21:10,435
[beeping] 

513
00:21:19,861 --> 00:21:21,571
[brakes screeching, car door opens]

514
00:21:21,655 --> 00:21:22,656
[car door slams shut]

515
00:21:27,536 --> 00:21:28,787
-Hi!
-[Colin] Hi.

516
00:21:28,870 --> 00:21:29,871
I'm Amanza.

517
00:21:29,955 --> 00:21:31,581
-Colin, nice to meet you.
-Nice to meet you, Colin.

518
00:21:31,665 --> 00:21:35,335
Sorry, I'm late. Crazy day, a little bit
last minute jumping in for Heather.

519
00:21:35,419 --> 00:21:37,421
She's at her boyfriend's
daughter's birthday.

520
00:21:37,504 --> 00:21:38,880
I've got two kids.

521
00:21:38,964 --> 00:21:41,675
My hair, like,  literally dried out
the window on the way here.

522
00:21:42,175 --> 00:21:43,635
-Make up in the car.
-I get it.

523
00:21:43,719 --> 00:21:45,220
-So, I'm here.
-I get it.

524
00:21:45,303 --> 00:21:47,597
Let's hope that this is worth the wait.

525
00:21:47,681 --> 00:21:50,309
The wait will be worth... the wait.
[laughing]

526
00:21:50,392 --> 00:21:52,477
-Perfect.
-The house will be worth the wait.

527
00:21:52,561 --> 00:21:53,687
I didn't plan on being late.

528
00:21:53,770 --> 00:21:57,607
I put in the time and I researched
the house and I'm ready to sell it.

529
00:21:58,191 --> 00:21:59,151
Nice.

530
00:21:59,234 --> 00:22:02,321
♪ Everybody watch now
I'mma do my thing ♪

531
00:22:07,200 --> 00:22:08,368
♪ Yeah, I'mma do my thing ♪

532
00:22:08,452 --> 00:22:09,578
[Amanza] Where do you live now?

533
00:22:09,661 --> 00:22:11,121
I live in downtown, actually.

534
00:22:11,204 --> 00:22:13,832
-So this is a really big transition.
-So...yeah.

535
00:22:13,915 --> 00:22:15,709
Going from a high-rise building.

536
00:22:15,792 --> 00:22:17,336
Everyone changes your light bulbs for you.

537
00:22:17,419 --> 00:22:19,296
-I'll have to do it myself.
-You're rowing up.

538
00:22:19,379 --> 00:22:20,881
So yeah, it's beautiful.

539
00:22:20,964 --> 00:22:23,300
-It's 3,100 square feet.
-[Colin] Okay.

540
00:22:23,383 --> 00:22:26,219
It's mid-century modern,
completely renovated.

541
00:22:26,303 --> 00:22:28,847
-I love how it's an open flow all the way.
-Oh, yeah.

542
00:22:31,016 --> 00:22:33,518
[Amanza] Beautiful Fleetwood doors
in the sunken living room.

543
00:22:33,602 --> 00:22:35,228
This is a pretty chill area.

544
00:22:35,312 --> 00:22:36,146
Are you a reader?

545
00:22:36,229 --> 00:22:38,440
-Plenty of built in bookshelves.
-I'm not a reader.

546
00:22:38,523 --> 00:22:41,443
They'll have to throw in the books
or it's gonna be bare and embarrassing.

547
00:22:41,526 --> 00:22:43,070
[Amanza] Do you cook at all?

548
00:22:43,153 --> 00:22:44,446
[Colin] I don't cook.

549
00:22:44,529 --> 00:22:48,033
[Amanza] There's a great kitchen in case
you have somebody to cook for you.

550
00:22:48,116 --> 00:22:49,534
The three bedrooms are this way.

551
00:22:51,119 --> 00:22:52,871
Let's have a look at the master.

552
00:22:52,954 --> 00:22:55,499
-Beautiful fireplace.
-[Colin] Nice. Another fireplace.

553
00:22:55,582 --> 00:22:58,335
Then the beautiful doors open up to...

554
00:22:58,418 --> 00:23:00,337
[Colin] The best part. Wow.

555
00:23:01,755 --> 00:23:03,507
It's great. It's your own little oasis.

556
00:23:03,924 --> 00:23:05,634
-It's so quiet, right?
-It's perfect.

557
00:23:05,717 --> 00:23:08,220
The flow is so just nice. You come out
the double doors in the back

558
00:23:08,303 --> 00:23:09,930
-and we're back in the living room.
-All right.

559
00:23:11,056 --> 00:23:13,100
-[Amanza] What do you think?
-I think it's great.

560
00:23:13,475 --> 00:23:14,768
I think that it's perfect.

561
00:23:15,018 --> 00:23:16,770
Heather will be happy to hear this.

562
00:23:17,062 --> 00:23:20,440
I may have been late, but I basically
landed this deal for Heather.

563
00:23:20,524 --> 00:23:22,484
So, you're welcome, Heather.

564
00:23:22,776 --> 00:23:23,944
-You did a good job.
-Nice.

565
00:23:24,027 --> 00:23:26,571
-Better late than never.
-Do I get Heather's commission?

566
00:23:26,655 --> 00:23:27,781
You guys can work that out.

567
00:23:38,125 --> 00:23:40,293
[ringing tone]

568
00:23:40,961 --> 00:23:42,963
Hey, Colin. It's Heather 
with the Oppenheim Group.

569
00:23:43,046 --> 00:23:45,257
-[Colin on phone] Hey. How are you?
-I'm good. How are you?

570
00:23:45,340 --> 00:23:46,925
[Colin] I'm great. How was the party?

571
00:23:47,968 --> 00:23:49,761
Um... [laughing]

572
00:23:50,387 --> 00:23:51,513
She told you about the party.

573
00:23:51,596 --> 00:23:55,851
Yeah, no. It was my boyfriend's
daughter's ninth birthday, so...

574
00:23:56,810 --> 00:23:59,813
Wow, really, Amanza?
You told him about my personal business?

575
00:23:59,980 --> 00:24:01,189
It's not cool at all.

576
00:24:01,273 --> 00:24:03,859
I think she's honestly
just sometimes in her own world

577
00:24:03,942 --> 00:24:05,944
and doesn't realize
that she has word vomit.

578
00:24:06,027 --> 00:24:08,321
She needs to be
a little bit more professional 

579
00:24:08,405 --> 00:24:10,407
and be careful what she says to people.

580
00:24:10,490 --> 00:24:12,492
The whole family was there and, uh...

581
00:24:13,326 --> 00:24:15,537
So, it was definitely something
I could not miss.

582
00:24:15,620 --> 00:24:18,832
You know, once again,
I apologize for Amanza being late.

583
00:24:18,915 --> 00:24:23,003
It wasn't the best impression,
so I'm really, really sorry about that.

584
00:24:23,503 --> 00:24:25,380
[Colin]
It's great Amanza was able to be there

585
00:24:25,464 --> 00:24:27,215
and I think we should put in an offer.

586
00:24:27,299 --> 00:24:28,884
You do? Awesome, okay.

587
00:24:28,967 --> 00:24:31,386
The asking price is 4.25.

588
00:24:31,470 --> 00:24:36,683
I'm thinking maybe we go in at, like, 
3.85, 3.9, somewhere around there.

589
00:24:36,892 --> 00:24:39,603
Yeah, I was kind of thinking
more, like, 3.7.

590
00:24:40,187 --> 00:24:42,189
Three-seven? Okay, well,

591
00:24:42,272 --> 00:24:43,773
I think it's an aggressive offer,

592
00:24:43,857 --> 00:24:46,943
but I can submit it and tell them 
that we're not gonna come in any higher.

593
00:24:47,027 --> 00:24:49,571
Don't get too excited, um...

594
00:24:49,654 --> 00:24:52,741
but let's be optimistic
and when I get to the office,

595
00:24:52,824 --> 00:24:56,036
I'm almost there, I will submit the offer
and then I'll keep you posted.

596
00:24:56,119 --> 00:24:58,121
[Colin] Sounds good,
I'll talk to you soon.

597
00:24:58,205 --> 00:24:59,956
Hopefully there's no more birthdays

598
00:25:00,040 --> 00:25:01,750
that come up
during the negotiation process.

599
00:25:02,834 --> 00:25:03,668
Yeah.

600
00:25:09,174 --> 00:25:11,092
♪ I've gone and hit the nail on the head ♪

601
00:25:11,176 --> 00:25:14,095
♪ Where did this break
Call it hashtag blessed ♪

602
00:25:14,513 --> 00:25:16,306
♪ I got it, I got it ♪

603
00:25:16,806 --> 00:25:18,725
♪ You want it, you want it ♪

604
00:25:20,018 --> 00:25:23,063
-[Brett] Look at that, man.
-Stay out of it.

605
00:25:23,146 --> 00:25:24,231
Come on, bro.

606
00:25:24,314 --> 00:25:26,608
♪ You keep it fly
I turn it up ♪

607
00:25:26,691 --> 00:25:29,236
♪ 'Cause what you have
It ain't enough ♪

608
00:25:29,319 --> 00:25:32,113
-[Mary] Hey, girl! You clean up well.
-[Amanza chuckling]

609
00:25:34,324 --> 00:25:36,701
-How are you? Hi!
-How are you?

610
00:25:36,785 --> 00:25:39,996
[Chrishell] Hi, beautiful.
Oh, my gosh, that's such a fun dress.

611
00:25:40,080 --> 00:25:41,164
[Mary] Oh, thank you.

612
00:25:41,248 --> 00:25:42,374
You know, let me try it.

613
00:25:42,999 --> 00:25:43,875
[cork pops]

614
00:25:43,959 --> 00:25:45,460
-[Jason] Boom.
-[Romain] Oh, my God.

615
00:25:45,543 --> 00:25:48,088
Who taught you how to open
a bottle of wine? Peel that thing off.

616
00:25:48,922 --> 00:25:50,131
[Romain sighs]

617
00:25:50,632 --> 00:25:52,634
♪ I got it, I got it ♪

618
00:25:52,717 --> 00:25:54,678
-[Heather] Hi.
-[Mary] How are you?

619
00:25:54,761 --> 00:25:56,972
-Hi, Romain.
-Hi.

620
00:25:57,055 --> 00:25:58,473
[Jason] Romain, Brett took the meat.

621
00:25:58,557 --> 00:26:01,059
[Mary] Did you just seriously
take the entire piece of meat?

622
00:26:01,184 --> 00:26:03,645
I did. I'm gonna give some to Romain, 
don't worry.

623
00:26:03,728 --> 00:26:05,105
Do you want some, too?

624
00:26:10,318 --> 00:26:11,778
-Mwah.
-[Christine] How are you?

625
00:26:11,861 --> 00:26:12,988
Good to see you!

626
00:26:14,698 --> 00:26:15,657
Don't mind if I do.

627
00:26:17,659 --> 00:26:18,618
[cork pops loudly]

628
00:26:18,702 --> 00:26:20,704
-[Brett] Jesus Christ!
-Sorry, I had to.

629
00:26:21,621 --> 00:26:23,957
[Brett] Can you warn me first 
before I lose an eye?

630
00:26:26,585 --> 00:26:28,253
[indistinct chattering]

631
00:26:29,754 --> 00:26:31,840
[Heather] It has, like, a good vibe
for, like, a house--

632
00:26:31,923 --> 00:26:34,217
[indistinct chatter]

633
00:26:34,301 --> 00:26:35,343
Trust fall.

634
00:26:35,885 --> 00:26:37,345
[Mary] At least
my other one made up for it.

635
00:26:37,429 --> 00:26:38,513
I know, right?

636
00:26:40,765 --> 00:26:42,350
-You good?
-Hi, Amanza.

637
00:26:42,559 --> 00:26:43,601
Good to see you.

638
00:26:43,852 --> 00:26:45,645
The beet salad is so good.

639
00:26:46,187 --> 00:26:48,023
[Mary] Jason is throwing a dinner party.

640
00:26:48,106 --> 00:26:50,525
This is just kind of what we do
at the Oppenheim Group.

641
00:26:50,609 --> 00:26:52,485
We're all very close, we're like family.

642
00:26:52,569 --> 00:26:55,113
But I'm still just kind of blown away

643
00:26:55,196 --> 00:26:57,282
by the fight that Christine and I had.

644
00:26:57,365 --> 00:27:00,535
I'm hoping that by keeping 
my distance from her,

645
00:27:00,619 --> 00:27:03,663
we can just make it through
this dinner in one piece.

646
00:27:04,080 --> 00:27:05,832
[Jason] Ladies, Brett, Romain,
let's cheers.

647
00:27:05,915 --> 00:27:08,168
For no reason at all
other than I love you guys.

648
00:27:08,251 --> 00:27:10,670
-[all] Aw!
-Cheers.

649
00:27:11,046 --> 00:27:11,921
Cheers.

650
00:27:12,005 --> 00:27:14,257
-[Heather] Love you guys.
-[Amanza] We love you, too.

651
00:27:14,591 --> 00:27:17,260
Oh, Heather, your client loved...

652
00:27:17,344 --> 00:27:18,845
[Heather] Yeah, he loves Doheny.

653
00:27:18,928 --> 00:27:21,264
-He was cool. He was really sweet.
-Yeah, Colin's amazing.

654
00:27:21,348 --> 00:27:23,016
He's gonna write an offer on it, so...

655
00:27:23,099 --> 00:27:24,768
-Good job.
-[Heather] I appreciate that.

656
00:27:24,851 --> 00:27:27,979
But Amanza was late to the showing.
[laughing]

657
00:27:28,813 --> 00:27:30,231
[Brett] How late are we talking?

658
00:27:30,649 --> 00:27:31,691
I honestly don't remember.

659
00:27:31,775 --> 00:27:32,859
Twenty-five, 30 minutes or so.

660
00:27:32,942 --> 00:27:36,571
I mean, yeah, I apologize,
but I have a lot going on,

661
00:27:36,655 --> 00:27:39,991
and I dropped, you know,
a lot that day to go help you.

662
00:27:40,075 --> 00:27:44,746
I think next time then,  just don't say
you'll do it if you can't show up on time.

663
00:27:44,829 --> 00:27:47,624
I didn't plan to not be on time.
[laughing]

664
00:27:47,707 --> 00:27:49,334
Nobody plans on being late, I know.

665
00:27:49,459 --> 00:27:52,587
[Jason] Tempered by the fact that
she was doing a favor and she's new...

666
00:27:52,921 --> 00:27:56,966
the point is made and I would be
a lot tougher on her in six months.

667
00:27:57,050 --> 00:27:58,885
And then, he also mentioned

668
00:27:58,968 --> 00:28:01,846
you told him
that I was at a birthday party, so...

669
00:28:01,930 --> 00:28:04,849
Just don't disclose
personal business, please.

670
00:28:04,933 --> 00:28:05,850
Um...

671
00:28:05,934 --> 00:28:08,061
I was there and it wasn't my showing,

672
00:28:08,144 --> 00:28:09,604
I was doing you a favor.

673
00:28:10,021 --> 00:28:10,939
I did my best.

674
00:28:11,022 --> 00:28:14,025
I think this girl has enough 
on her plate, too.

675
00:28:14,109 --> 00:28:18,321
-She's a single mother right now.
-We're all balancing a lot.

676
00:28:18,405 --> 00:28:20,907
It doesn't matter if it's, like,
a birthday party...

677
00:28:20,990 --> 00:28:22,575
Like, kids-- We all have a lot going on.

678
00:28:22,659 --> 00:28:24,744
Why don't you have Amanza show 
all your showings,

679
00:28:24,828 --> 00:28:26,413
and then you can just do what you want.

680
00:28:26,496 --> 00:28:28,748
It's about being professional 
for work, though.

681
00:28:28,873 --> 00:28:29,999
You were at a birthday party.

682
00:28:30,083 --> 00:28:32,752
Don't clap back at me that,
"I'm at a birthday party."

683
00:28:32,836 --> 00:28:35,130
I asked for a favor
and you said you would do it.

684
00:28:35,213 --> 00:28:37,424
[Brett] Drop the mic, Heather.
It's not worth it. It's not worth it.

685
00:28:37,507 --> 00:28:40,593
[Mary] You guys have the luxury
of having nannies and everything.

686
00:28:40,677 --> 00:28:41,720
Oh, Mary.

687
00:28:42,303 --> 00:28:44,180
[Heather] Don't bring that into it.

688
00:28:44,264 --> 00:28:47,434
If you have a nanny, you have money,
then yeah, you can do a lot.

689
00:28:47,517 --> 00:28:50,061
But if you don't, things are not easy.

690
00:28:50,145 --> 00:28:52,772
For her to give Amanza 
so much crap about it,

691
00:28:53,148 --> 00:28:55,066
I think she's in for a rude awakening.

692
00:28:55,150 --> 00:28:58,486
Mary, you're defending her
because she's your best friend.

693
00:28:58,570 --> 00:28:59,612
[Mary] I am.

694
00:28:59,696 --> 00:29:01,698
She's also going through a lot right now.

695
00:29:01,823 --> 00:29:03,867
That's also another thing.

696
00:29:03,950 --> 00:29:06,327
Don't make me feel guilty
because I went to my

